-- See `Widget.yana`: a second `Widget.describe`, so an importer of both has an ambiguity rather
-- than an import order - the namespaced half of `findDotOverloads`'s own answer.
--
-- Over a `Widget` of this module's own. Adding to `Widget.yana`'s would be the namespace rule's
-- refusal (modules.md, "Namespaces", `Reject.Namespace.Foreign.yana`) rather than an ambiguity, and
-- a module is allowed to declare a type whose name another module also uses.

pub data Widget {size: Int}

pub fn Widget.describe(self: Widget) -> Int = 2
